 ;; Fields a person or a Principal tunes. Class Fields come from the schema; these are the rest.
 :fields {"instructions/charter" "What a Principal is for. Part of its system prompt, written first."
          "instructions/own" "A Principal's own standing notes to itself, part of its system prompt."
          "memory/notes" "What a Principal keeps between wakes, in its own words. Serialized on every wake, up to memory/budget."
          "memory/budget" "How many tokens of memory/notes a wake carries."
          "memory/policy" "How a Principal should use its memory, in plain words."
          "serialize/budget-tokens" "The prompt budget of one model call, estimated at 4 chars per token."
          "serialize/compress-at" "Tokens of unsummarised conversation at which a wake compresses first. Unset: 70 percent of what the budget leaves after the standing prompt. 0 turns compression off."
          "serialize/summary-tokens" "The size a conversation's summary should stay under, in tokens. Unset: 400."
          "serialize/compressor" "The prompt that writes a conversation's summary. Unset: the shipped one."
          "loop/max-iterations" "Turns a wake may take before one last turn with no tools. Unset: 8."
          "loop/max-ops" "Ops a Principal may make in one turn. Unset: 16."
          "loop/reasoning" "Whether this Principal's model reasons: on, off, or inherit from its Model."
          "loop/accepts-from" "Who may wake this Principal."
          "policy/approval" "Which ops wait for a person's card. A person's own session changes it, nobody else."
          "policy/approval-rules" "Standing rules that admit gated ops without a card, each with a Task as record."
          "policy/unsafe" "Unsafe mode on this Principal: no cards until it expires. Changed only through approval.unsafe and approval.unsafe.off."
          "world/unsafe" "Every armed Principal and unconfined Adapter. Any session may read it; it drives the red indicator."
          "world/notifications" "Where notifications live. Any session may read it."
          "world/manual" "Where this manual lives. Any session may read it."
          "world/release" "The release this world is running: commit, version, log version."
          "object/label" "A pretty name for people. Agents keep resolving the bound name."}}
